  "behavior": [
    "Replace the blanket 38% spin loss on every impact with body-frame contact normal and friction impulses using the actual posed lever and contact velocity.",
    "Preserve no-slip rolling and unrelated spin; skip contacts already swinging away. Bound angular gain to 85% of kinetic energy removed by the authoritative linear rebound and retain the 16 rad/s cap.",
    "Shared helper scratch storage avoids per-contact allocations. Translation, collision counters, recovery clocks and gameplay randomness retain their ownership.",
    "Cache small directional hulls for quantized skin-weight groups to retain blended cloth surfaces exposed by bent hips/thighs; continue sparse posed sampling, with no full per-frame skin scan.",
    "Add Next impact to advance the same lab incident to its next collision. Keep bounded contact traces and separate gameplay hashes in the profiling harness."
  ],
